in our series the new normal we look at  how the pandemic is dramatically  changing  our everyday lives this morning how an  ancient setting was turned into a safe  performance space  centuries ago rome's circus maximus was  where romans gathered to watch  chariot races today in the era of social  distancing chris livesay shows  us how modern romans are heading there  once again  for a night at the opera  the art form is synonymous with italy  but the setting is out of place and time  more than 2 000 years ago it was chariot  races that drew romans here to the  circus  maximus today it's opening night of  verdi's rigoletto  reinterpreted with a 1970s setting  but the audience is unmistakably from  2020  safely seated more than six feet apart  something the rome opera couldn't  achieve inside its concert hall  or at its smaller outdoor venue  soprano rosa feola says the circus  maximus  spanning more than two football fields  is a godsend  it's been four months that we are not  allowed to sing  in theaters because it's not safe place  so  we was waiting for this moment to come  back to the life  again so i feel like a very young young  young singer  again a young singer in an  old place with a history of charismatic  performers  [Music]  now picture it this is the same  racetrack where emperor nero himself  would  race chariot before 150 000  screaming romans now today because of  social distancing and coronavirus  it's only 1500 spectators here at the  opera  seeing verdi in such a historic setting  is moving after all these months in  lockdown  says one opera goer  is life you know and we need to live and  we need  the art even the set was designed with  social distancing in mind  when you have the the energy to go  through a person you have a car  in the middle so you remember that you  have not to go the other side with the  singing with the music  you can give emotions even if we are not  touching if there's going to be a second  act  even opera can adapt  for cbs this morning chris livesay roam  gosh you heard that piece i want to hear  more yeah i know it's so great to see a  live performance if it takes parking  cars on the stage to keep people apart  great whatever works being creative
 

